---
import BaseLayout from "@/components/layout/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About AI Career Guide"
  description="Learn about the mission and editorial approach behind AI Career Guide."
>
  <div class="legal-page-premium max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-[var(--color-text-primary)]">
      About AI Career Guide
    </h1>
    <div
      class="mt-8 prose prose-lg max-w-none
  text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]
  prose-headings:text-[var(--color-text-primary)]
  prose-a:text-[var(--color-accent)] prose-a:no-underline hover:prose-a:underline
  prose-strong:text-[var(--color-text-primary)]
  prose-ul:text-[var(--color-text-secondary)] prose-ol:text-[var(--color-text-secondary)] marker:text-[var(--color-text-muted)]"
    >
      <p>
        <strong>AI Career Guide</strong> is a global English-language learning and
        career publication for students, developers, and early-career builders working
        toward AI, machine learning, software engineering, and modern AI application
        development.
      </p>
      <p>
        Everything is organized around one progression: <strong
          >Learn → Build → Prove</strong
        >. Learn the fundamentals in the right order, build real systems,
        evaluate what you build, and turn that work into evidence of your
        ability.
      </p>
      <p>
        The goal is not to help readers collect courses, frameworks, or trendy
        tools. It is to help them make better technical decisions, develop
        durable fundamentals, and build a portfolio that demonstrates real
        engineering ability.
      </p>
      <h2>What the site covers</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>AI & ML</strong> – Machine learning, deep learning, LLMs, generative
          AI, AI engineering.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Career</strong> – Role guidance, roadmaps, interview preparation,
          portfolio strategy, and career decision-making.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Projects</strong> – Hands‑on tutorials from beginner to advanced.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Tools</strong> – Curated lists and reviews of AI and developer tools.
        </li>
        <li><strong>Resources</strong> – Books, courses, datasets, APIs.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>How we aim to stay trustworthy</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Technical claims should be supported by reliable sources.</li>
        <li>Meaningful changes should be reflected in updated dates.</li>
        <li>
          Errors and outdated references should be corrected when identified.
        </li>
        <li>
          Affiliate relationships should be disclosed and should not control
          technical conclusions.
        </li>
        <li>
          The site does not require a newsletter subscription or account to
          access core educational content.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <h2>What we will not optimize for</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Publishing large volumes of low-value, search-first content.</li>
        <li>
          Recommending a tool simply because it is popular, sponsored, or pays
          more.
        </li>
        <li>
          Using intrusive ads, deceptive links, or interfaces designed to create
          accidental clicks.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <h2>How the site may make money</h2>
      <p>
        AI Career Guide may eventually use standard display advertising, clearly
        disclosed affiliate links, and selected sponsorships. Commercial
        relationships should not determine technical conclusions or editorial
        recommendations. Any sponsored or affiliate relationship will be
        disclosed on the relevant page.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you have any questions, suggestions, or collaboration ideas, please <a
          href="/contact">get in touch</a
        >.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
